# Line endings are part of the contract, not of the checkout (ADR-001 K3).
# A bash script carried to a Linux server with CRLF fails on its first line; core.autocrlf on a
# Windows workstation would hand it CRLF. So scripts and the files the resolver and drivers read
# are LF everywhere; PowerShell runs either way and stays LF too, for one rule.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.jar binary
